{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And it shall be on the seventh day, he shall shave.</b> What grew during those seven days — and he would perform two shavings." "<b>All his hair, his head.</b> But regarding the Levites it says only ״והעבירו תער על כל בשרם״ — meaning, they shall pass a razor over the flesh of all of them, in the manner of those who shave for adornment around the head and the beard and the eyebrows, shaving part and leaving the majority, for if you say they were to shave off all the hair, they would come in dishevelment before the Shekhinah. But as for lepers — were it possible to strip the skin off their flesh while they are alive, the verse would have required them to do so, because of the tsara'at that had spread on their skin." "<b>All his hair.</b> What does Scripture mean by <b>he shall shave</b>? To impose responsibility for the shaving — that if he did not shave on the seventh day, he shaves on the eighth, the ninth, and the tenth."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "Reading נְווּלִים as 'dishevelment'; the word may carry connotations of disgrace or disfigurement in this context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:11.780592214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}